※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 8501 IMPL_BACKEND_UNSUPPORTED

※ Nothing in the language writes a value of a product or a sum yet, so a
※ function that takes or answers with one is a function the compiler has
※ nothing to generate.  It says so rather than putting the value in a register
※ it does not fit in.

type Point = x : f64 ; y : f64

@[visible]
fn middle(p: Point) → Point:
    p

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    0u8
